e night.\n\nThe whispers became a voice. It knew Maya Chen's name. It offered a deal: leave Blackwood House, leave a mirror that shows another room, and walk away clean. Maya Chen considered it for exactly as long as it took to be afraid — then refused."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Night', 'text': 'It came on the anniversary, as Maya Chen knew it would. The fog pressed against the windows of Blackwood House like a face. a mirror that shows another room activated — played, filled, showed, rang, drew, unlocked — and the Hollow Man stepped out of the walls.\n\nthe skeptic Dr. Lane arrived — of course the skeptic Dr. Lane did, called by the thing friends are — with headlights and a crowbar and no plan at all. Together they forced the Hollow Man back toward the nursery, toward a mirror that shows another room, toward the broken place.\n\nMaya Chen understood then what had to be done: not destroy a mirror that shows another room, but complete it. Join the halves. Speak the name. Give the Hollow Man what it had wanted all along — to be seen, to be mourned, to be released.'}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'Aftermath', 'text': "a mirror that shows another room, mended, sits on the mantel. It doesn't play, or fill, or show. It's just an object now — which is to say, it's just a story. Maya Chen keeps it to remember: courage is a light.\n\nThe archives got a new entry, in Maya Chen's handwriting: what happened, what worked, what it cost. Let the next tenant know. Let no one ever pretend again.\n\nBlackwood House is for sale again, and Maya Chen is staying. Someone has to be here who knows. Someone has to keep the light on. That someone is Maya Chen now."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Epilogue: The Light Kept', 'text': "the skeptic Dr. Lane visits every anniversary with pancakes and bad jokes. They don't talk about that night. They don't need to. It's in the walls — but the walls, now, are just walls.\n\nYears later, Maya Chen still walks Blackwood House at night, checking the rooms the way you check 